<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Varduli</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 19 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A people of the western Pyrenean coast in Gipuzkoa and Álava, among the ancestors of the Basques.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Varduli lived in the area of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gipuzkoa">Gipuzkoa</a> and parts of Álava and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> in the later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a>, between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/caristii">Caristii</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vascones">Vascones</a>. Whether they spoke an early form of Basque or a Celtic language is debated.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of their society. They lived from herding, farming, fishing and the iron of their hills, and Ptolemy names towns such as Gebala and Menosca. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a> includes them among the rough mountain peoples of the north.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>They came under Roman rule as part of the conquest of the north completed in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cantabrian-wars">Cantabrian Wars</a> of 19 BCE, and later supplied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/auxilia">auxiliary troops</a>, including a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cohort">cohort</a> of Varduli that served in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>. Their land became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hispania-tarraconensis">Hispania Tarraconensis</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 300 BCE – 19 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:53.73%;width:5.59%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 19 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Vardulians</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-160&amp;focus=varduli" aria-label="Varduli on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4627 741 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Varduli lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5031 967h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4947 997h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4947 997h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Spain. <a href="/atlas?year=-160&amp;focus=varduli">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
